    "entry": "2026-09-18 — overseer-b85-bwp3: shared documentation surfaces are a shared file",
    "quote": "Documentation surfaces that a repository's conventions say every task must update are a shared file for the rule that chains tasks touching the same file, and are easy to miss because a batch can look parallel on its code while every task updates the same documents: either chain the tasks so each branches from a batch branch carrying the previous task's documentation, or give the documentation update to a single closing task and say so in every other task's description."
  },
